<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <!--
    Spring Boot 3.3.x is the line that pairs with Java 21 and is what the
    eclipse-temurin:21 images run. The scaffold proposed a 4.x parent and
    three artifact ids that do not exist in Maven Central
    (spring-boot-starter-webmvc, -webmvc-test, -actuator-test). Those were
    replaced with the real ones: spring-boot-starter-web and
    spring-boot-starter-test.
  -->
  <parent>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
    <version>3.3.5</version>
    <relativePath/>
  </parent>

  <groupId>com.example</groupId>
  <artifactId>app</artifactId>
  <version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
  <name>gitops-monorepo-app</name>
  <description>Release-mode demo service for the GitOps monorepo platform</description>

  <properties>
    <java.version>21</java.version>
    <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>

    <!--
      CVE PATCH LEVELS — these override the versions the Boot 3.3.5 BOM pins.

      WHY THESE EXIST: Boot 3.3.5 was released in Nov 2024. Its BOM freezes
      tomcat-embed and spring-framework at that date, and the image scan
      (HIGH/CRITICAL, fixed-only, before push) found accumulated advisories
      against both:

        tomcat-embed-core   CVE-2024-50379  RCE, TOCTOU in JSP compilation
                            CVE-2024-56337  incomplete fix for the above
                            CVE-2025-48988  DoS, multipart upload
                            CVE-2025-48989  DoS, HTTP/2 "MadeYouReset"
                            CVE-2025-52520  DoS
                            CVE-2025-53506  DoS
                            CVE-2025-55752  directory traversal, possible RCE
                            CVE-2026-24734  certificate revocation bypass
        spring-expression   CVE-2026-41850  DoS via crafted SpEL
        spring-webmvc       CVE-2026-41842  DoS resolving static resources
                            CVE-2026-41845  XSS, incorrect JavaScript escaping

      WHY OVERRIDE PROPERTIES RATHER THAN BUMP THE PARENT: moving to a newer
      Boot minor would pull these transitively, but this repo has already lost
      three CI attempts to asserting external version identifiers that could
      not be verified from the build environment. These two numbers were NOT
      guessed — Trivy printed them itself in the "Fixed Version" column of the
      failing run. Overriding the Boot BOM's own properties is the supported
      mechanism (spring-boot-dependencies declares both), so the whole
      dependency tree moves coherently and requireUpperBoundDeps in the lint
      stage will fail the build if anything is left behind.

      MAINTENANCE: when the parent is next raised, DELETE these two
      properties rather than carrying them forward — a stale downgrade-pin is
      worse than none. The lint stage's enforcer catches the conflict.
    -->
    <tomcat.version>10.1.52</tomcat.version>
    <spring-framework.version>6.2.19</spring-framework.version>
  </properties>

  <dependencies>
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!-- Health endpoint, remapped to /healthz in application.properties. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!--
      Without this, actuator's prometheus endpoint does not exist and the
      ServiceScrapes in gitops/scrapes/ would scrape a 404 forever.
      NOTE: the dependency alone is not sufficient — the endpoint must also be
      ENABLED in application.properties. Exposure is not enablement; that
      distinction cost two CI attempts.
    -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>io.micrometer</groupId>
      <artifactId>micrometer-registry-prometheus</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
      <scope>test</scope>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <finalName>app</finalName>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
